## annelid women's weekly

*2016 · Mingji Liu*

**Ingredient:**

-   Four packets of horsehair worms (or thin, viscous tube worms)*

-   Two chopped earthworms, with clitellum scooped out

-   One chopped trematode flatworm, also de-glanded

-   Fresh salad life: baby worm, redworm, baby periproct

-   Hokkien soy sauce

-   Two tbsp of ragworm flakes

-   One tbsp of leech spice

-   Priapulid oil

-   Half a cup of sediment cysts

**For a non-nematomorpha option, replace with giant Gippsland worms and gluten-free soy sauce.*

**Serves:** Friends

**Instructions:**

1.  Discard the desiccated, arthropod hosts that came with horsehair worms.

2.  Thanks.

3.  Break horsehairs into small pieces. Boil them until tender.

4.  Run horsehairs under cold water in colander and drain.

5.  Put cold horsehairs in salad bowl. Apply generous amounts of priapulid oil and sediment cysts.

6.  Mix.

7.  Add earthworms, flatworms, and salad life.

8.  Toss.

9.  Add ragworm flakes, leech spice, and a wash of soy.

10. Toss.

11. Reflect upon the fragile, segmented beauty of their bodies.

12. Enjoy.

## Coming across a confidante's profile on a dating website (61% match, 20% enemy) on Wednesday night and all of a sudden my chest feels tight. I resist the urge to click on it and all those awful feelings return -- that aching pain that she will never want what I have to give.

*2016 · Mingji Liu*

**This is a poem about garlic bread.**

O tender, garlic-washed meal,  
Swaddled in steaming foil.  
How I love its soft mouth-feel,  
Its salts and virgin olive oil.

Centrepiece of the party plate,  
Scoured and scattered to a crumb,  
No other nibble can be as great.  
Serve it all. I want to feel numb.

***G **reat!*  
***A **romatic!*  
***R **evolutionary!*  
***L **icktacular!*  
***I **t-tastes-so-good!*  
***C **runchy!*

Such a heady, herb-topped snack,  
Concocted for the ravenous addict.  
Only $1.90 in a Coles twin pack --  
Why does it get to be so perfect?

Prepared with an oven's kiss,  
It soars above the culinary tides.  
I take in all its chewy bliss  
To fill my aching, wounded sides.

***B **rave!*  
***R **edeemable!*  
***E **ngaged!*  
***A **dult!*  
***D **oes-not-skip-therapy!  
*  
Done it now, mate. You're out of spit.  
Someone with teeth's gonna find this,  
Realise you're pathetic and unfit,  
Glare from the kitchen  
and they'll hiss:

"Mingji, you're such a piece of shit."

If only I could broil my head...  
If only I could grill my soul...  
So like cheap, fucking garlic bread,  
It too becomes acceptable and whole.

## Consort

*2016 · Mingji Liu*

Lament, Artemisia, lament!  
Rake your grief  
Across bloodless riverbeds.  
Pour your drought  
Into the swollen  
Hills of Caria.  
Let your heatwave of want  
Drain the fields from  
Lycia to Phygia,  
From Pisidia to  
AAAAH FUCK --

Lament, sister-wife, lament!  
Smear his ashes,  
Black as widowhood,  
To your broken lip.  
Dissolve his body  
In trembling wine and  
Gorge it into the  
Mausoleum of  
Your own.

Serve all your subjects  
This ghoulish,  
Nail-tearing thirst.  
Your courtiers, eunuchs,  
Dancers, oracles,  
Emissaries of Persia,  
Make them taste what it feels like  
To lose an earth entire.  
Make them all know  
All know

OH GOD NO --

And know that  
No matter how grand  
An elegy is written,  
No matter how high  
The marble has risen,

He will never come back.  
Not ever.

## Crow letter.

*2016 · Mingji Liu*

Saw a dead crow today --

Stop 26 outside royal park station --  
Broken black brolly -- discarded in wet grass --  
Face -- shame covered -- a defeated wing --  
No more baby noise -- no more beady hops --  
Just a dead crow in child's resting pose.

Sick of orange pill -- nauseous stomach empty --  
No more acetaminophen -- goodbye wine on friday --  
Tired from keeping in -- wired with instant coffee --  
Old with lips on weekends -- cold from sushi lunches  --

Sometimes I just -- sometimes I just --  
I don't know.

Saw a crow eating crow today --  
The feast was silent -- his chest was lonely  --  
Could taste its tarry strings -- dark bitter feathers --  
They ate each other up -- inside it ate its brother --  
Saw a crow eat another -- I saw it and I wept.

## Culinary nuts

*2016 · Mingji Liu*

Peanut.  
Arachis hypogaea.  
Or groundnut.

Today, I discover  
You are not a nut.

Peanut.  
A grain legume.  
Leguminosae.

But peanut.  
I knew you.  
How can this be?

Peanut.  
Crop of lies.  
Peanut.  
Judas pea.  
Peanut.  
Trollop spread.  
Peanut.  
Jezebel's snack.

And yet, this meal  
of mendacity grows.

Brazil nut.  
An angiosperm, not a nut.  
Pine nut.  
A gymnosperm, not a nut.  
Walnut.  
A drupe, not a nut.

I have eaten falsehoods  
for far too long.

I weep for you,  
Peanut.  
Truly, I do.

Peanut.  
Very tasty.  
Not a nut.

## Dido, grief of Carthage

*2016 · Mingji Liu*

***Dido, grief of Carthage  ***  
Or:** *recollections of a panic attack in mid-sep 2015***

Trapped in a fever dream,  
down the whirlpool,  
oh oh oh i scream.  
why do i tread water at your party,  
encircled by wine-dark sirens  
singing their galley-slave ditty  
while my hands are tied to this glass of gin?  
why didn't you greet me like you did  
to that girl with the pearl-face grin  
and flower hot name,  
or notice  
my silk summer frame  
and pink roses i wear just for you?  
why won't you stroke my ragged claws,  
the cockles and cowries i accrue,  
or touch my mermaid hair so wet?  
you must see my bones are coral made,  
my heart a sinking drift net.  
you Cetus.  
you brute.  
why has time beset us  
such that even when i am certain

@@@@

your long white arms  
will never touch me again,  
i still feel your scalding charms?  
oh how my fly ash failures rush to me  
like wicked djinn  
stinging with endless glee  
inside my tindered brain!  
i once tried to cast your embrace  
into the ruby depths of Jahannam  
by writing my disgrace  
into a desperate letter  
and striking it with a redhead match.  
i wanted every second i thought you better  
destroyed upon a flickering page.  
but still my mind forges  
this pig iron cage,  
where you and i  
melt in the crucible of your backyard,  
into rivulets of shame and alkali,  
sludge and longing and

%%%%

sinkholes of desire,  
pitch-dark  
with hollow bulbs and viscid mire.  
i fear that if i linger in this false home  
any longer i will be buried  
alive under the clay, the loam,  
the pebble, the peat,  
of leached and tunnelled panic,  
with only dwarfs and serpents to greet.  
but tonight will not fester like that dance  
at the beer hall  
when you toyed my advance  
for three fucking hours,  
and ...oh gods no...  
the way you were thralled by her powers,  
the way she made smile,  
the way you kept drinking and drinking at her,  
as my stomach turned to wood  
and the roots of Yggdrasil  
gnawed into my trembling skin  
like a hand-spun drill.  
now my hands won't stop trembling from the

&&&&

cold change in the night  
as i stagger out of your party.  
my chest is a paper kite  
fluttering like coloured prayers...  
like a banished cloud  
alone in the Himalayas...  
but i swear upon lines of the Bardo Thodol  
these lustful winds will no longer  
exact such a scarring toll.  
i cannot keep battering my back  
with these beastly garuda wings.  
i am distressed and i am a wrack  
of pain and sometimes i call on aerial  
beings like vultures and crows  
to consume me in a cacophonous sky burial.  
but no no no no!  
deep inside i know this gale will pass,  
i know my maladies will blow  
off the cliff as my bosom comes to rest.  
i am willing to fly everything to make this right.  
i am going to pass this test.

####

Aeneas. You know my sorrow.  
But please do not think of me.  
It will pass with each tomorrow.

## Eagle.

*2016 · Mingji Liu*

Eagle

Floats above the floating world,  
Alone,  
A watcher,  
A cresting wave of talon.

Two great wings,  
A pair of shields  
Beating,  
Wind-lanced and shadow.

Two black eyes,  
Fleeting,  
Spying the rock  
And veined mountain snow.

Soars above a soaring world,  
Alone,  
A hunter,  
Arrowhead at dawn.

A screeching dive. The rush of knives.  
A shriek of feathers. The water shatters.

Bursts from the lake  
With thrashing flesh,  
Pink and torsional,  
Like tallow between his claws.

Silently takes his prize,  
Blood-wet fresh.  
His beak is etched,  
Sky-battered and raw.

Eagle

Pierces the land with a single glare.  
Alone.  
His throne,  
The frozen, whistling air.

## First frost

*2016 · Mingji Liu*

Here it turns a face again --  
Father bitters of the earth.  
Blades to milky crunch,  
Icy worm begat in footy  
Cleat holes. Night salted,  
Sod locks, a daguerrotype  
Morning. Hold me in this  
Memory and Desire field.  
