*"Pa claimed he was terrified of the cosmos. At least, that's what he started saying towards the end. He'd close his eyes -- bury his entire face in his pillow, in fact -- and start mumbling about stars and comets and asteroids. About how they were going to swallow him entire. I didn't know what to make of it at the time.*

*Before long, that was all Pa ever seemed to speak about. I'd drive to the hospice every night to visit, and all I could do was sit at his bedside, as patient as the moon, while he ranted and raved about outer space.*

