## How to succeed

*2016 · Mingji Liu*

**How to succeed **at business without really trying.

STEP ONE

Bury your **wallet** in sour grass.  
Retch into a **briefcase.**  
Keel onto night slops and  
Smear kaka over your **cufflinks.  
**  
STEP TWO  
  
Crawl into a **pitch**-hole.  
Take **stock** of its dampness.  
Do not move for seven hours,  
Until a **network **of mould grows inside you.**  
**  
STEP THREE

Shovel gravel into your mouth.  
Gasp at the **efficient **pain.  
**Synergise** the jaw until  
A gorgeous slug of blood **slides** down your chin.

STEP FOUR

Climb the citadel.  
Toss **business cards **into the vortex.  
Beseech towers above and gods below  
That no **stakeholder** sees you and calls you faggot.

STEP FIVE

All the while you weep and wail and  
**Grow** with sobbing despair at  
The passing of earth.  
This strong, masculine earth.

## I Ching

*2016 · Mingji Liu*

In those ancient, green-bronzed, semi-terracotta times,

The King would beseech the Oracles of Court with Great

Questions of His Time:

*"Should the Kingdom march against the North?"*

*"Shall Peace be forged through marriage or blood?"*

*"Where should the summer palace be built and in what month should I go elephant hunting?"*

In those ancient, jade-faced, knife-coined times,

The Oracle would cast turtle shells in a chalice of fire,

And read the cracks in the ashen shell,

To render fortune out of heavenly woe.

The drums of war,

The fate of the countless,

The rise of wonders,

And fall of nations,

Such was foretold by the Oracle.

Even today,

